    <section id="consultation" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>4. Consultation intake and consent</h2>
        <p>The online consultation forms are for adults aged 18 or older seeking consultation at the wellness center. Scanning a QR code opens the form; it does not book an appointment or create a clinician–patient relationship. Submitting a form requests review and does not guarantee acceptance, a diagnosis, treatment, or a response within a particular time.</p>
        <p>Provide information about yourself honestly and as accurately as you can. Use available unknown or prefer-not-to-answer choices when appropriate. Do not invent measurements or laboratory results. Tell center staff about errors, changes in symptoms, and information you could not provide online. This online workflow does not support submissions for children or a separate guardian-consent process.</p>
        <p>Before submitting, you must affirmatively consent to collecting and clinically reviewing your health information, including automated screening flags. You may choose not to submit and speak with staff about other consultation arrangements. Read the <a href="/privacy#consultation-consent">Privacy Policy</a> for access, correction, retention and consent choices. Do not put medical histories or sensitive records in the general contact form or order notes.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="screening" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>5. Screening flags and clinical review</h2>
        <p>Screening uses predefined rules applied to your answers. It is not a diagnosis, a validated estimate of your individual disease probability, or a replacement for assessment by a qualified clinician. Missing or inaccurate answers can affect the result; both false alarms and missed concerns are possible.</p>
        <p>Blue indicates informational or incomplete-data flags, yellow indicates a follow-up concern, orange indicates a higher-priority concern, and red indicates an urgent concern. Labels and explanations accompany colors. Green is a reviewer-selected status meaning “Reviewed — no outstanding action”; it is not an automated declaration that you are disease-free. Original screening flags remain part of the submitted record.</p>
        <p>Only an authorized clinical reviewer can interpret the results in context and decide what further assessment is appropriate. Do not start, stop, or change medication based on a flag. Ask staff for an explanation or correction if information appears wrong.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="emergencies" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>6. Emergencies and service interruptions</h2>
        <p>This website is not an emergency service and submissions are not monitored continuously. An urgent flag does not call an ambulance, alert emergency services, or guarantee immediate clinician contact. For severe or rapidly worsening symptoms, or immediate risk of harm, seek urgent local medical assistance rather than waiting for an online response.</p>
        <p>A connection interruption may temporarily lock an interactive page while it reconnects. Unsubmitted answers may be recovered during a short reconnection window, but recovery is not guaranteed. Reloading, closing the page, or an expired session can discard an unfinished form. Only a successful submission confirmation means the form has been saved. If unsure whether a submission succeeded, ask center staff before entering it again.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="products" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>7. Product information and availability</h2>
        <p>We aim to present product descriptions, images, prices, package sizes, and availability accurately, but information may change and errors may occur. Displaying an item does not guarantee that it is available, approved in your jurisdiction, or suitable for you.</p>
        <p>Consult a qualified healthcare professional before using a supplement, especially if you are pregnant, nursing, under 18, have a medical condition, or take medication. Follow final product labels and instructions.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="orders" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>8. Order requests, quotes, and payments</h2>
        <p>Checkout submits an order request for review. No payment is collected at that step. A VitalReach representative confirms availability, shipping, applicable taxes, and the final total before payment becomes available. Review the confirmed quote and payment currency before paying through the hosted Stripe or Paystack checkout. Payment status is updated after verification with the provider. Contact us with your order number for questions about your order, cancellation, or a refund.</p>
        <p>Do not send card numbers, bank credentials, government identification numbers, or other sensitive financial information through ordinary email or website inquiry fields.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="administrators" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>9. Administrator accounts</h2>
        <p>The administration portal is limited to users approved in the VitalReach access database. Google authenticates administrator identity; VitalReach determines authorization. Administrators must use their own account, protect their Google account, and notify us promptly of suspected unauthorized access.</p>
        <p>We may disable or remove administrator access when needed to protect the website, data, users, or VitalReach operations. Administrators may only access and change information for authorized VitalReach purposes.</p>
    <p>Clinical records require a separate clinical-reviewer permission in addition to an active administrator account. Superadministrator permission allows access management but does not itself grant clinical access. Clinical record access and review actions are audited. Reviewers must act within their professional qualifications, independently assess screening flags, protect confidentiality, and use records only for authorized care and operational purposes.</p>
    </section>

